• Identify regions with higher energy potential density;
• Cross-reference data with the location of active infrastructure in the State;
• Support feasibility studies for new academic research or ventures in the renewable energy sector.

• Compare classes and sub-residues: evaluate the viability of multiple materials together;
• Map process losses: understand the impact of each factor in the transition from theoretical to real potential;
• Simulate custom scenarios: adjust the percentages of each variable to reflect your plant's operational reality;
• Project sensitivity: contrast multiple market and productivity scenarios for the same feedstock.

1. Select Waste: In the left menu, choose the class and sub-residues to include in the simulation;
2. Define the Scenario: In the center of the screen, select the reference scenario most aligned with your objective;
3. Choose Visualization: Choose one of the 4 available graphical display modes to analyze the results;
4. Adjust Parameters: In the panel next to the chart, customize factor percentages based on your data sources.

• Evaluate the techno-economic feasibility of biogas and bioproduct projects;
• Estimate the investment payback period;
• Project the annual volume of biogas generated based on biomass availability.

1. Identify yourself: enter your name, email and municipality, and consent to the use of your data (LGPD);
2. Select the residue: Choose the biomass of interest for sizing;
3. Enter the volume: Provide the annual availability (in tons/year) or planted area (in hectares);
4. Define the harvest season: Indicate crop seasonality distribution across the months;
5. Choose product and calculate: Select the desired bioproduct and click to calculate potential and view financial indicators.
